   Installation Procedures
   ========================
       Read the following information before you begin to install
       LANtastic V6.0.

     Memory Requirements
     -------------------
       Before you install LANtastic, make sure you have 510K of DOS memory
       available to run the installation, its Extract function or the
       SETUP utility.
  
     Upgrading from V5.0 with LANCACHE
     ---------------------------------
       If you are upgrading your LANtastic software from V5.0 or earlier to
       V6.0 and choose to "KEEP" your current system files and settings, 
       you may need to modify your network startup batch file so that 
       LANCACHE loads before SERVER.  The LANCACHE program that ships with 
       LANtastic V6.0 will not load if it detects that the SERVER program 
       is already running.

     Procedure for Upgrading Windows-based LANtastic
     -----------------------------------------------
       If you're performing an upgrade installation on a computer that's
       running LANtastic's Windows interface, move all program items
       that aren't part of the LANtastic installation to a program group
       other than LANtastic.  This includes items such as Voice Error
       Messaging, LAN Radio and ArtiScribe, as well as any non-LANtastic
       program items such as E-Mail icons.  Any program items that are
       left in the LANtastic program group will be removed from it during
       the LANtastic installation.  You'll be able to re-assign the
       removed items to the LANtastic program group through Program
       Manager once the installation is complete.

     Adding or Removing the LANtastic Menu
     -------------------------------------
       In a new LANtastic installation, a LANtastic menu appears on the
       Windows File Manager menu line. From this menu, you can access all
       the functions available from the LANtastic Net window by scrolling
       down the list and selecting the desired menu option. To add this
       functionality to a LANtastic upgrade installation, or to remove
       it from an existing installation, use a text editor such as Windows
       Notepad or DOS EDIT to add or remove the following line to the
       [AddOns] section of your WINFILE.INI file:

                 LANtastic for File Manager=C:\LANTASTI\LFFMEXT.DLL

       where C:\LANTASTI is your LANtastic installation directory.

     NDIS Adapter Driver Diskette
     ----------------------------
       If you select NDIS Supported Adapter during the LANtastic
       installation, you'll need to have your adapter's driver diskette
       ready to insert when prompted to do so.

     SMB/NCP Installation
     --------------------
       If you selected SMB and/or NCP-client support during the LANtastic
       installation, you are ready to connect to and use SMB and /or
       NCP servers and their resources.  File modifications that may be
       mentioned in the LANtastic Installation and Management Guide
       shouldn't be needed unless there was a problem during the
       installation.  However, you must have NETBEUI.EXE in your LANtastic
       installation directory to be able to communicate with SMB servers.
       Contact Microsoft to obtain NETBEUI.EXE.  See the on-line manual
       and the LANtastic Installation and Management Guide for information
       on setting up SMB and/or NCP-client support manually.

       NOTES  NodeRunner adapters must be run in 16-bit mode to connect
              to NCP or SMB servers.

              Simply LANtastic network adapters are not compatible with
              NCP or SMB networks.

       You can set up a drive or printer connection to an SMB or NCP
       server only if:

          - The name for a printer begins with an "@" symbol.
          - The drive or printer name doesn't contain any spaces.
          - SMB drives don't have passwords.

       After installation you can set up drive and printer connections
       that don't meet these criteria by editing STARTNET.BAT and adding
       NET commands such as:

              NET LOGIN "\\WFW SERVER"
              NET USE D: "\\WFW SERVER\CDRIVE" SECRET
              NET USE LPT1 "\\WFW SERVER\HP" HPSECRET

       Note: Arguments to NET that contain spaces must be in double
             quotes.

     New AI-NDIS Line
     ----------------
       The documentation that describes NCP client support may give an
       incorrect AI-NDIS command line example.  An example of the correct
       syntax for the NDIS line is:

              AI-NDIS BIND_TO=NRODI NO_RECEIVE_HOLDOFF RECEIVE_BUFFERS=4

     Using the LANSETUP Program
     --------------------------
       After you install LANtastic V6.0, you can use the LANSETUP program
       to:

         - View your system setup
         - Reset the control directory
         - Add default resources
         - Enable or disable sharing of your printers and drives
         - Enable or disable LANtastic
         - View the LANtastic V6.0 On-line Manual

       To use the LANSETUP program:

         - In DOS, type LANSETUP <Enter> from the DOS prompt in the
           LANTASTI directory.

         - In Windows, choose the LANtastic Setup icon in the LANtastic
           Program Group.

   Installing Over a Previous LANtastic NDIS Installation
   ======================================================
       If you have LANtastic already installed on a computer using an
       NDIS network adapter driver, see the following scenarios for
       important steps to take before installing LANtastic V6.0.

           If you don't plan to install NDIS, NCP or SMB support, use a
           text editor such as DOS EDIT or Windows Notepad to remove the
           DEVICE=PROTMAN.DOS and NDIS adapter driver lines from your
           CONFIG.SYS file.

           If you plan to install NDIS and/or SMB support using the same
           network adapter driver, you don't need to make any changes.

           If you plan to install NCP support or use an adapter driver
           other than the one used in your previous LANtastic
           installation, use a text editor such as DOS EDIT or Windows
           Notepad to remove the adapter driver line from your CONFIG.SYS
           file.

      The PROTMAN.DOS line and most NDIS adapter driver lines usually
      begin with a DEVICE= statement and end with the extension .DOS.

      Once these steps have been completed, install LANtastic V6.0 as
      described in the LANtastic Installation and Management Guide.

   Using the LANtastic On-line Manual
   ====================================
       Included in your LANtastic installation directory is the LANtastic
       V6.0 On-line Manual.  This manual contains information about the
       following topics:

          - LANtastic Commands and Switches
          - LANtastic NDIS Support
          - Using Control Directories with DOS
          - LANtastic SMB Support
          - DOS and Application Program Considerations
          - Using Multiple Adapters
          - Using Artisoft's IPX Routable NetBIOS
          - Indirect Files
          - Physical Access ACL
          - The NBSETUP program

       To use the on-line manual, change to your installation directory
       (usually C:\LANTASTI.) From within the LANtastic installation
       directory, change to the ARTIDOCS directory and and type:

                     ARTIDOCS

       An introduction screen appears. Press the Esc key to see the main
       menu.  Choose the desired topic from the menu and press Enter.

    Copying and Pasting Accounts, ACL Groups and Resources
    =======================================================
       When copying and pasting multiple individual accounts, ACL groups
       or resources using wildcard characters, the "To Account," "To
       Group" or "To Resource" name will always match the "From Account,"
       "From Group" or "From Resource" name, including wildcard
       characters.

    Using Linkbook
    ==============
       You must have at least three megabytes of free RAM (Random
       Access Memory) before you run Linkbook. This is in addition to the
       memory required for DDE applications. You can check the amount of
       free memory by choosing About Program Manager from the Help menu in
       Windows Program Manager. The available memory can be either
       physical or virtual.

     Establishing DDE Links Using Microsoft Excel V5.0
     --------------------------------------------------
       Excel V5.0 may return a timeout error message during paste link
       operations when it's used as the DDE server. A DDE server is 
       the computer running the application that placed the item in the 
       clipboard.  The problem occurs when a paste link operation is 
       performed on a client after pasting from a remote clipboard 
       containing Excel V5.0 data. The timeout error message is due to 
       inconsistent registration entries in the WIN.REG file for Excel 
       versions. For a temporary solution to this problem, complete 
       the following steps:

          1. From Program Manager's File menu, choose Run.

          2. In the Command Line field of the Run window, type REGEDIT.EXE
             and press Enter.  The Registration Info Editor appears.

          3. Scroll down through the list of applications until you
             see the entries for Microsoft Excel.

          4. Delete each Excel entry. To delete an entry, select it with
             the mouse, then press the Delete key.

       This operation won't affect installed Excel versions using DDE or
       OLE.  Continue with the operation as instructed in your LANtastic
       and Excel manuals.

     Using LINKBOOK with Microsoft Word 2.0
     --------------------------------------
       When opening a DDE client Microsoft Word V2.0 document that has
       links to a Word V2.0 document on another computer (the DDE server),
       you must use one of these two configurations:

       A.  Make sure that Word V2.0 is not running on the DDE server but
           is in the server's DOS path variable.

                                      OR

       B.  Make sure that Word V2.0 is running on the server and that the
           linked document is opened in a window.

     Launching Applications with Linkbook
     ------------------------------------
       If you're using Linkbook to launch an application on a remote
       server, you must be sure that the DOS path statement on that server
       includes the directory that contains the desired application.

     Multiple Adapters
     -----------------
       If multiple adapters are installed in your computer, the Paste
       Remote Clipboard command can only be used to access workstations
       that are connected to adapter #0.

   Server Startup Parameters
   =========================
       The LANtastic Installation and Management Guide may contain
       incorrect information about the Configuration Type field in the
       Server Startup Parameters.  The example configuration types, "Small
       File Server" and "Small File and Print Server,"etc. are not valid
       options.  Instead, you're able to choose between 5, 35 or 100 User
       File Server or File and Print Server configuration types.

   Connecting to SMB/NCP Servers
   =============================
       To access files on an SMB or NCP server, you must redirect a
       drive letter to the server's drives or printers. No network path
       access is available.

       Also, when logging in to a SMB or NCP server, your computer may
       beep several times before the connection is made. This occurs as
       the redirector automatically tries each protocol and adapter until
       the server responds. If you have many adapters and SMB and NCP
       support enabled, it may take as long as 15 seconds for some
       connections.

       See the on-line manual for examples of batch files used to connect
       to SMB and NCP servers.

     Turning Off Autodisconnect
     --------------------------
       In Windows(TM) NT(R), inactive connections are terminated after a
       time interval specified by the Autodisconnect command (the default
       is 20 minutes). An inactive connection is one that has transferred
       no data for the specified interval. To increase the interval,
       change the default value for the disc setting in the Registry. To
       do this complete these steps on the Windows NT server:

         1. Choose Run from the File menu.

         2. Type REGEDT32 and press Enter. The HKEY folders appear.

         3. Click on the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE folder to bring it to the
            foreground.

         4. Choose System.

         5. Choose Current Control Set.

         6. Choose Services.

         7. Scroll down to Lanman Server and choose it.

         8. Choose Parameters.

         9. Choose disc: REG_DWORD:nnnnnnn. The DWORD Editor opens.
            Enter a new time interval. If you don't want your connections
            to terminate automatically, enter ffffffff.

         For more information, see your Windows NT Resource Kit.

   Using Novell's NETX with LANtastic NCP Support
   ==============================================
       To use Novell's NETX program with LANtastic's NCP support, complete
       these steps:

         1. Use a text editor such as DOS EDIT or Windows Notepad to
            remove the NCP_SUPPORT line from the REDIR section of the
            STARTNET.CFG file.

         2. Check your LANtastic startup batch file (usually STARTNET.BAT)
            to be certain that all of your LANtastic drive and printer
            connections are made before NETX is loaded.  Your computer
            will lock up if you attempt to run the LANtastic NET program
            while NETX is running.

   Controlling a Remote Server
   ===========================
       When you're controlling a remote server using the DOS NET or
       Windows LANtastic Net programs, avoid using the command "SERVER
       /REMOVE" to shut down the SERVER program.  Instead use the remote
       server shutdown feature, described in "Remotely Shutting Down a
       Server" in the Server Monitoring and Security chapter in your
       LANtastic Installation and Management Guide.

   Using DOS EDIT.COM
   ==================
       Don't run DOS EDIT.COM while controlling a remote server.
       Keystrokes entered on the controlling computer aren't accepted by
       EDIT.  EDIT will also lock up your computer if you attempt to
       reboot your computer by pressing Ctrl+Alt+Del while running both
       LANtastic's SERVER program and DOS EDIT.

   Using LANtastic with Stacker
   ============================
       If you are installing LANtastic on a drive that has been compressed
       using the Stacker utility and you want that computer to be a
       server, an Artisoft Exchange Mail Post Office or an installation
       server, complete the steps below.  If the computer will not share
       its drives or printers and will not run the LANtastic SERVER
       program, these steps are not necessary.

              1.  After the LANtastic installation, delete the control
                  directory as described in the LANtastic Installation and
                  Management Guide.

              2.  On a drive that has not been compressed using Stacker,
                  create a new control directory as described in the
                  LANtastic Installation and Management Guide.

   Using NET PING
   ==============
       The NET PING command can report the same workstation multiple
       times.  This is often true on networks with long delays or slow
       nodes. To get a list of nodes without repeated entries, pipe NET
       PING to the DOS SORT command and redirect the output to a file.
       Then use a text editor to identify and remove multiple appearances
       of the same node. For example:

              NET PING | SORT >PING.TXT
              EDIT PING.TXT

       You can use wildcard characters to limit the number of nodes that
       will respond to the NET PING command. For example:

              NET PING A*
              NET PING B*

   Using Artisoft Drivers with LANtastic Interchange
   =================================================
       The Artisoft drivers shipped with LANtastic V6.0 (NODERUN.EXE,
       NR.EXE, AEX.EXE, AI-NDIS.EXE) aren't compatible with LANtastic
       Interchange V1.0

       The older versions of these drivers (those that shipped with
       LANtastic V5.0 and LANtastic Interchange) can be used on a V 6.0
       node to make it compatible with LANtastic Interchange.

       If you install LANtastic V6.0 after you've installed LANtastic
       Interchange, you must then reinstall LANtastic Interchange. This
       reloads the older drivers.

   New Error Messages
   ==================
       If the error message "Unable to complete installation process"
       appears while you're attempting to perform a LANtastic installation
       on a computer that's running Windows, you don't have enough
       memory to run the installation program under Windows.  To install
       LANtastic on this computer, complete these steps:

           1.  Make certain that Windows isn't running on the computer
               and that you have at least 490 K DOS memory available.

           2.  From the DOS prompt, type:

                     A:INSTALL/DOS/WIN

               The installation program will now run under DOS but will
               install all of LANtastic's Windows functions.

           3.  Complete the installation as directed in your LANtastic
               Installation and Management Guide.

       The error message "Required system component not installed" lets you
       know that a computer is attempting to access a portion of the
       server's SERVER program that has been disabled using the LANtastic
       Server Startup Parameters.  See your LANtastic Installation
       and Management Guide for information on enabling and disabling
       SERVER modules.

   Command Line Switches
   =====================
       The LANtastic Installation and Management Guide may list an invalid
       range of available values for the FILES= command line switch.  The
       correct range of available values is 50 - 5100.  The default
       value of 0 tells the SERVER program to use the value specified in
       the CONFIG.SYS file.

       A list of command line switches that are not included in your 
       LANtastic Installation and Management Guide appears below.  For 
       complete information on LANtastic's command line switches, see 
       the on-line manual.

       REDIR Switches
       --------------
         DISCONNECT_NORETRY   Prevents automatic reconnection to a server
                              when you are disconnected.

       SERVER Switches
       ---------------
         PARK                 Parks the hard drive when the LANtastic
                              SERVER program is shut down.

       AI-NDIS Switches
       ----------------
         NO-RECEIVE_HOLDOFF   Used for compatibility with ODINSUP and NCP
                              support.

